# Conditional arena for online typed-body selection

This isolated implementation fixes logical register addresses before any
classical online choice. It accepts actual frozen source REG, bounded-content
VOTE, rejected-size VOTE and overlay lookup factories. It does not accept
caller-supplied resource reports or arbitrary emitter callbacks. This is a
conditional component composition interface, not the complete adaptive proof
game, physical workspace qualification, or an accepted security assumption.

The preceding source audit is `target/parliament-adaptive-entry-audit/README.md`.
Owner acceptance and independent cryptographic review remain open. Production
gates are unchanged. Captures use an isolated historical source root because
the live Cargo manifest no longer matches the frozen source catalog; neither
the historical catalog nor earlier receipts are repinned.

## Explicit parameters and scope

`Budget` requires row, valid-body cap T, invalid-typed-body cap I, external
combined lookup cap Q, message cap C, encoded length width b, rejected-length
envelope J, explicit `conservative-total-calls` log policy, and names asserting
one immutable F and its agreed total completion. It requires T+I<=2^64,
0<=J<=2^64-1, 6882996<=C<2^b, 1<=b<=4096 and finite nonnegative Q. These are
proposal inputs and extra finite-experiment restrictions, not adopted theorem
constants. No invalid cap is inferred from valid-only T; Q does not bound C or
establish the cryptographic theorem's oracle-query convention.

The one-row arena uses M=2^20 and N=(T+I)(M+2). All W and L0 costs are recomputed
at N,b. This conservatively reserves M+2 for each potential generating body,
including invalid public content. No invalid-call reservation is refunded.
S=T+I=0 explicitly skips all request-family construction and supports the
actual zero-log lookup factory. Its unused two-bit counter is still charged.
The capacity guarantee requires the shared log and counter to be initially
zero. The shared work region K must be initially zero and boundary-clean after
each atomic component. External operations must not write the log, counter or
work, and must not access private coin/purifier banks or future private banks.
Only the bound source components may update shared internal state, under their
actual source contracts and canonical full-support input premises. A nonempty
initial log or external append is outside this capacity guarantee.

`bind_reg` requires a same-row typed PublicShape with body0..4096 and six
contexts0..256. `bind_vote` requires n3..1000 and chooses actual ContentFamily.
`bind_rejected` requires n<=J outside3..1000 and retains all3608+1024n borrowed
input bits. A mathematical u64 length bound does not attest native Vec
reachability. `rejected_witness` obtains an attaining popcount maximum using J
and its cleared-bit/all-lower-ones candidates, filtered to rejected lengths,
plus0/1/2. The elementary rejected maximum is5881+2popcount(witness); J itself
need not attain it.

Every binding explicitly supplies one of the documented entry-premise
constants. They are **not checked admission proofs**. Valid requests require
public and application/witness validity upstream. Invalid bounded VOTE means
the component's public-invalid content contract, not public-valid but
witness-invalid input. Raw parsing errors, witness failures, optional helpers,
application/context work and direct verification remain unknown external
paths. Unsupported labels/shapes are refused rather than priced at zero.
Query binding likewise requires canonical length<=C and zero padding on the
full coherent support, source domain zero padding and the same immutable F.

## Arena and counts

`Plan` is immutable and represents huge caps by arithmetic intervals, never a
list of all experiment slots. With S=T+I, it reserves a shared log/counter,
S disjoint public/coin/output/purifier slots, Q disjoint query/enable/output
slots, and one maximum boundary-clean work region. Per-row source role maxima
give P*,R*,O*; K dominates retained_G+max(Gscratch,Wwork,Ework), rejected
workspace519, and L0 workspace when Q>0. Thus the known wire count is

    N(1+b+8*215150+2112) + max(2,bit_length(N))
      + S(P*+2R*+O*) + Q(b+8C+1+2112) + K.

Each chosen component's actual original input is split into public and private
coin intervals. Source schema checks locate original iv_pre/salt and every
other coin, not their derived aliases. Varying a public shape does not move
coins, earlier outputs, future slots, or shared scratch. All local wires are
covered by an injective Relocation; variable-F spans cannot cross a split.
REG/VOTE return encodings remain typed subviews of O*, not a new shared wire
format. Caller state preparation/routing and control/trace storage are unpriced.

The known coordinatewise body upper is T*V_g+I*J_g+Q*L0_g. It retains a separate
scalar elementary upper obtained from the correct per-family elementary
maxima. REG's exact X maximum4095/255 and elementary maximum4096/256 are not
conflated; the synthetic upper vector retains X+CX+5CCX convention. Each
external combined lookup costs two base F calls, in addition to each request's
own base calls. No implementation cost or quantum state size of F is included.

## Online lifecycle and freshness premise

`OnlineArena` exposes a read-only fixed plan and immutable retained chosen
trace. A factory binding checks caps, source identity, actual component
metadata, coin schema, geometry and relocation before committing counters or
the trace. Only the next chosen call is emitted. A subsequent shape can be
chosen after the preceding stream is consumed; no later binding relabels an
earlier gate. Pending or abandoned streams block further selections.

All S maximum banks have R* private original coins and R* retained purifiers.
The fixed preparation stream emits S*R* H and S*R* CNOT gates, including unused
banks. `emit_preparation()` reserves that lifecycle immediately; merely
obtaining or partially consuming its lazy iterator does not open body entry.
Full consumption opens it, or `acknowledge_prepared_banks(PREPARED)` records an
explicit supplied Bell-state premise. Neither path checks quantum states or
proves physical execution. Initial freshness/product state, private future-bank
noninterference and boundary-clean scratch remain requirements.

For the explicit H/CX construction, `coin_and_purifier_initial_zero_bits=2SR*`
counts the coin/purifier registers only. The separate initially clean internal
budget is log_bits+counter_bits+K; their sum is
`explicit_preparation_total_internal_zero_bits`. Caller public/query inputs and
arbitrary XOR targets are excluded from these zero-input counts. These are
logical zero-state requirements, not initialization/reset costs or execution
evidence. With a supplied Bell-state acknowledgment, coins and purifiers are
already in that required state; the explicit construction's zero count is not
a claim that those supplied Bell registers are zero. Shared log/counter/work
zero-state and noninterference premises remain mandatory in either mode.

Conditionally, induction on classical histories leaves untouched future banks
independent of the entering cq state; selected prefixes have the required
uniform mixed marginals when their purifiers are traced. This does not price a
classical controller, implement a coherent selector, or establish the full
joint quantum theorem. No conditioning on a completed trace is used.

`emit_chosen_inverse()` reverses the retained chosen component order and each
actual component inverse. It excludes external input preparation, selection,
measurements and controller history, and leaves coin/purifier preparation in
place. Stream exhaustion is bookkeeping, not proof gates were executed. The
source API assumes Python interpreter/module memory integrity; private-field
tampering, hostile monkeypatches and concurrent file edits are outside that
contract. Before/after file and exact module-origin checks are drift controls,
not a hostile runtime attestation mechanism.

## Validation and remaining work

Focused controls use real source factories. Full rejected-size circuits run in
an independent sparse Boolean interpreter with output-driven next selection
and a true retained-trace inverse. REG and bounded-content VOTE are full-M
factory metadata and short emitted-prefix checks; their enormous complete
streams are not executed. Other controls cover zero-log queries, separate cap
refusal before mutation, fixed addresses at huge caps, rejected popcount
boundaries/exhaustive small caps, preparation/atomic lifecycle, source drift,
and dependency origins outside the expected directory suffix. Capture receipts
record exact collection/execution membership and frozen source identities.

